course: dictionary
lesson: 14824
title: Quilts and quilting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A quilt is a warm bed cover. It is made of two layers of cloth with soft stuffing between them, and it is often stitched in a pattern. «Grandma kept us warm under her quilt on cold nights.»
explain: Quilt can also be a verb. To quilt means to sew layers of cloth together with stitches. «She quilted the layers together with neat lines of stitches.» The clues tell you which meaning is used: the word after quilt is a thing you sew, not a thing you sleep under.
explain: A patchwork quilt is made from many small pieces of cloth sewn together. «Each square of the patchwork quilt came from an old shirt.» The squares make a pattern, so you can count them in rows and columns, just like in maths.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you think quilt means a bed cover, does «Grandma kept us warm under her bed cover on cold nights» still make sense? It does, so you are right.
fact: A quilt is a warm bed cover made of two layers of cloth with soft stuffing between them.
fact: To quilt means to sew layers of cloth together with stitches in lines or patterns.
fact: A patchwork quilt is made from many small pieces of cloth sewn together.
fact: In the UK, «quilt» is another word for a duvet.
fact: A quilt of squares in rows and columns is like an array: rows × squares in each row = total squares.
exercise: «Grandma kept us warm under her quilt on cold nights.» What is a quilt here? | A pair of stitches | *A warm bed cover | A kind of cold wind | A small piece of cloth
exercise: «She quilted the jacket with neat stitches in lines.» What does quilted mean here? | Torn into small pieces | Folded very small | Painted in bright colours | *Sewn in layers with stitches
exercise: «Each square of the patchwork quilt came from an old shirt.» What is a patchwork quilt made from? | *Many small pieces of cloth sewn together | Old shoes and hats | One large sheet of paper | A single stitched pattern in one colour
test: In maths, a quilt has 3 rows with 6 squares in each row. How many squares are there altogether? | *18 | 12 | 9 | 24
test: In the UK, what else is a quilt called? | A curtain | A pillow | A blanket for the car | *A duvet
exam: Which sentence uses quilt as a verb? | *«They will quilt the layers together this afternoon.» | «It was a patchwork quilt from Grandma.» | «The quilt was warm and soft.»
